     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and I don't know of any indication for metformin at 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled dose, and the harm it can cause, mainly lactic acidosis, can be severe.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that right away, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Get a pharmacist or attending review.** If there is a documented reason to exceed the maximum, such as a protocol or specialist recommendation, the order can go through your hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **Check the number.** If 1700 mg was meant as a total daily dose, I can enter it as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
